 linked helper expansion. Conflicting local/workgroup allocations and pointers with
 no single descriptor root retain their typed call boundary. No new reflection or
 source-proof fields are needed, but translation/cache identities must change.
+
+A branch-local numeric entry-buffer read without an unconditional accessible span
+can be evaluated under its original branch condition, then reconverged before the
+sampling selection. The native typed transform builds guarded address/read blocks
+and phi values with zero on inactive paths; the original descriptor operations,
+samples and side effects keep their source sites. This is conditional evaluation,
+not storage-load speculation. It requires single-predecessor source arms, static
+entry-rooted address paths and a prefix free of writes, calls, barriers and ordered
+reads. The CFG/derivative pass still proves uniformity and matching loop instances.
+Unsupported shapes remain visible refusals. Direct, linked and cached paths share
+the resulting dominating values without additional source-proof metadata.
